is strictly slower. An arithmetic progression of errors does not go to zero unless the common difference is zero.","preview":["newton-local-quadratic-convergence"],"figure":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 340 176\" role=\"img\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\"><title>a line sloping down</title><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"318\" y2=\"146\"/><polygon points=\"318,146 311.6,148.7 311.6,143.3\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"46\" y2=\"24\"/><polygon points=\"46,24 48.7,30.4 43.3,30.4\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"318\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">t</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"20\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">z</text><polyline points=\"46,39 49,40.1 52,41.1 55.1,42.1 58.1,43.2 61.1,44.2 64.1,45.3 67.2,46.3 70.2,47.4 73.2,48.4 76.2,49.4 79.2,50.5 82.3,51.5 85.3,52.6 88.3,53.6 91.3,54.7 94.4,55.7 97.4,56.7 100.4,57.8 103.4,58.8 106.4,59.9 109.5,60.9 112.5,62 115.5,63 118.5,64 121.6,65.1 124.6,66.1 127.6,67.2 130.6,68.2 133.6,69.3 136.7,70.3 139.7,71.3 142.7,72.4 145.7,73.4 148.8,74.5 151.8,75.5 154.8,76.6 157.8,77.6 160.8,78.6 163.9,79.7 166.9,80.7 169.9,81.8 172.9,82.8 176,83.9 179,84.9 182,85.9 185,87 188,88 191.1,89.1 194.1,90.1 197.1,91.2 200.1,92.2 203.2,93.2 206.2,94.3 209.2,95.3 212.2,96.4 215.2,97.4 218.3,98.5 221.3,99.5 224.3,100.5 227.3,101.6 230.4,102.6 233.4,103.7 236.4,104.7 239.4,105.8 242.4,106.8 245.5,107.8 248.5,108.9 251.5,109.9 254.5,111 257.6,112 260.6,113 263.6,114.1 266.6,115.1 269.6,116.2 272.7,117.2 275.7,118.3 278.7,119.3 281.7,120.3 284.8,121.4 287.8,122.4 290.8,123.5 293.8,124.5 296.8,125.6 299.9,126.6 302.9,127.6 305.9,128.7 308.9,129.7 312,130.8 315,131.8 318,132.9\" stroke-width=\"2.2\"/></svg>","figure_alt":"A straight line sloping downward on labeled axes."},{"id":"convergence-rates-r4-q2","version":1,"round":4,"type":"numeric","prompt":"Two successive errors are \\(0.05\\) and \\(0.01\\), and the same ratio continues. What is \\(e_{k+1}/e_k\\)?","answer":0.2,"unit":"1","tolerance":0.02,"explanation":"Divide \\(0.01\\) by \\(0.05\\). The quotient is \\(1/5 = 0.2\\). That constant in \\((0, 1)\\) is a linear rate. Reporting \\(5\\) inverts the ratio. Reporting \\(0.04\\) is the difference of the two errors. Reporting \\(0.01\\) repeats the later error.","preview":["condition-number-gradient-rate"],"figure":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 340 176\" role=\"img\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\"><title>a falling curve</title><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"318\" y2=\"146\"/><polygon points=\"318,146 311.6,148.7 311.6,143.3\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"46\" y2=\"24\"/><polygon points=\"46,24 48.7,30.4 43.3,30.4\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"318\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">k</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"20\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">e</text><polyline points=\"46,39 49,41.9 52,44.8 55.1,47.5 58.1,50.2 61.1,52.8 64.1,55.3 67.2,57.7 70.2,60.1 73.2,62.4 76.2,64.6 79.2,66.8 82.3,68.9 85.3,71 88.3,73 91.3,74.9 94.4,76.8 97.4,78.6 100.4,80.4 103.4,82.1 106.4,83.8 109.5,85.4 112.5,87 115.5,88.5 118.5,90 121.6,91.4 124.6,92.8 127.6,94.2 130.6,95.5 133.6,96.8 136.7,98.1 139.7,99.3 142.7,100.4 145.7,101.6 148.8,102.7 151.8,103.8 154.8,104.8 157.8,105.8 160.8,106.8 163.9,107.8 166.9,108.7 169.9,109.6 172.9,110.5 176,111.4 179,112.2 182,113 185,113.8 188,114.5 191.1,115.3 194.1,116 197.1,116.7 200.1,117.4 203.2,118 206.2,118.7 209.2,119.3 212.2,119.9 215.2,120.5 218.3,121 221.3,121.6 224.3,122.1 227.3,122.6 230.4,123.1 233.4,123.6 236.4,124.1 239.4,124.6 242.4,125 245.